  "Which of the following statements is true?\nA. A To secure the conversion option on a bond, bondholders would pay a reduced (i.e. discounted) bond price.\nB. B Typically, the conversion ratio is set so that the firm's stock price must appreciate at least 40 percent before it is profitable to convert bonds into stock.\nC. C A convertible bond is issued by government agencies rather than a firm with stock.\nD. D Convertible bonds can be converted into shares of common stock at some predetermined ratio at the discretion of the bondholder.\nD",
