  "Which of the following statements is true of annual percentage rate (APR)?\nA. A The Truth-in-Savings Act was passed by Congress to ensure that the true cost of credit was disclosed to consumers.\nB. B The Truth-in-Lending Act was passed to provide consumers an accurate estimate of the return they would earn on an investment.\nC. C The Truth-in-Savings Act and Truth-in-Lending Act require by law that the APR be disclosed on all consumer loans and savings plans.\nD. D The annual percentage rate (APR), and not the effective annual interest rate (EAR), represents the true economic interest rate.\nC",
